+## Implemented public surface
+
+API generation 29 adds one sealed factory persistence owner through `registerReviewPersistence({ open, write })`.
+The shared controller validates and restores native human checkpoints for an exact canonical checkout, immutable owner review ID, and ordered document identity.
+Native keyboard and mouse saves await the owner's write before publishing saved state or note events.
+Failures keep the composer text and a persistent warning, and unreadable or foreign checkpoints cannot be overwritten by subsequent saves.
+Checkpoints include saved human IDs, original provenance/anchors, native status, unsaved composer mode/text, semantic selection, and review identity.
+Draft/selection writes serialize with human saves and transitions; graceful shutdown waits before retiring extension storage resources.
+Public command controls expose `checkpoint`, `setNoteStatus`, and guarded `requestReload`, including detached patch bytes and exact-revision note acknowledgements.
+Acknowledgement releases transition protection without resolving notes; later edits invalidate an old captured revision, and saving an edit reopens a resolved note.
+Shared reconciliation classifies changed context/source as stale and absent addressed context or files as orphaned, without relocating original anchors.
+Unavailable-file notes remain valid in snapshots and ordinary live-session registration.
+The session wire revision is 17, with the v17 fixture generated by the owned generator and the v16 fixture removed.
+Local checkpoints are not a second session protocol.
+
+## Public native proof
+
+`test/pty/review-persistence-integration.test.ts` drives the source CLI through the repository isolated PTY harness and ordinary public extension/session controls.
+The scenarios cover rejected writes, acknowledged keyboard and mouse saves, typing during an outstanding write, identity-preserving editable human restoration, immutable review switching, protected/open/resolved status, stale context, vanished-file inventory, and public daemon registration.
+They also cover SIGKILL recovery of a draft on the second selected file, continued native typing, forged provenance, foreign checkout/review/document identity, concurrent composer and source-editor rejection, acknowledgement invalidation after edits, reopening a resolved note, canonical checkout retention from a subdirectory, and keyboard ownership after blank-save closure.
+Storage fault injection lives in the public extension-owned port, without mocking the shared store or calling private daemon APIs.
+Fixtures demonstrate host acknowledgement and recovery behavior; atomic storage and physical durability remain the persistence owner's implementation responsibility.
+
+Red regressions preceded their repairs at the public seam.
+The unavailable-file baseline inventory produced zero saved notes rather than one (`.bun-tmp/inventory-red.log`).
+The restored-context case accepted forged provenance before validation (`.bun-tmp/restore-adversarial-red.log`).
+Acknowledged revisions initially returned `ACK failed`, resolved edits remained resolved, inline transitions changed the checkout root to a nested directory, and blank closure swallowed review keys (`host-acknowledgement-red.log`, `host-reopen-red.log`, `host-root-red.log`, and `host-blank-save-red.log` under `.bun-tmp`).
+Their corresponding green checks use the same public commands and native UI flows.
+The initial persistence slices also failed before factory registration and native restoration existed, then passed after the awaited controller path landed.
