+### Preserved invariants
+
+`ReviewController.prepare` reads and validates restoration without acquiring durable writing authority.
+AppHost validates the outgoing ticket, completes its synchronous producer/broker/publication commit, retires the outgoing controller, and exposes the incoming loading state before its initialization acknowledges storage.
+A source editor or composer that changes while candidate reads await invalidates the ticket without any incoming write.
+After publication, native input stays unavailable during acknowledgement; there is no outgoing mutation window across the awaited write.
+A failed mounted adoption keeps restored human state and a visible warning, refuses saves, and permits an ordinary explicit refresh to retry with the same read-time authority.
+It never refreshes a competing CAS version or retries another viewer's payload.
+
+Integration writer keys include immutable review ID, checkout, document identity, and publication generation.
+Only the failed first-acknowledgement binding is released; successfully acknowledged outgoing bindings remain independent.
+Opening a candidate does not clear the mounted readiness checkpoint, and subsequent mounted writes update that checkpoint even after a canceled candidate read.
+Lifecycle readiness additionally requires the actual acknowledged writer for the newly opened owner, so a failed same-factory adoption cannot borrow the old view's readiness checkpoint.
+Saved human IDs, original provenance/anchors, note dispositions, selection, and composer semantics remain native.
+API generation 29, checkpoint version 1, session wire 17, consecutive producer generations, whole-checkpoint equality/no-op flush guards, and lifecycle `ctx.review` containing only `requestReload` remain unchanged.
+No public fields or controller shapes were injected into event contexts.
