+## Durable native human review persistence (API 29)
+
+When an extension must restore native human notes or protect automatic review replacement, read `docs/turn-review-host-interface.md` and the durable persistence section of `docs/extensions.md` before implementation.
+Register one `registerReviewPersistence({ open, write })` owner during factory registration.
+Bind storage to the host's canonical checkout and exact ordered document identity; return an immutable review ID and only that review's prior checkpoint.
+Resolve `write` only after durable storage acknowledges the complete immutable checkpoint.
+Use command-time `ctx.review.checkpoint()`, `setNoteStatus(noteId, status, expected)`, and `requestReload({ mode, expected, source, acknowledgedNotes })` through the public facade.
+Preserve original human IDs, anchors, provenance, status, and drafts; do not synthesize agent comments or call private daemon endpoints to restore them.
+Treat `busy`, `protected`, and `conflict` results as refused transitions, and retain the current review rather than retrying with a fabricated revision.
+Storage/read failures remain visible and prevent overwriting unreadable checkpoints.
+Acknowledge captured saved note IDs only after the owner durably preserves or submits their exact revisions; this releases transition protection without resolving notes, and later edits invalidate the expected revision.
+Owner storage, history selection, and feedback delivery remain extension responsibilities; the host handles semantic state and durable native save acknowledgement.
